  "ai_summary": "Devs aren't entirely cooked, though recent shifts show divergence. IT consultancy stocks are collapsing (-26.7% YoY, -15.1% 30-day), pricing in AI automation of outsourced work. Conversely, Indeed software dev job postings show strong 1-year growth (+22.8%) alongside neutral 30-day gains (+3.3%). Big Tech headcounts show mixed cuts (Meta down 14.8% YoY, flat 30-day), while AI labs like Anthropic avoid hoarding freezes, adding 57 jobs in 30 days. Are devs cooked? Well, AI labs are hiring while consultancy stocks plummet, proving the robots want to write code, but they still need humans to update Jira.",
